### Daily consumption max power (mesure_synchrone_auto/v2). Per Enedis, the metering APIs cannot be
### tested in the sandbox (it returns placeholder dates such as 20XX-XX-XX), so these requests target
### PROD ({{ENEDIS_API_PROD}}). 99999999999999 is a placeholder: replace it with a real PRM whose
### holder has consented to your application, and set a real PROD token in
### http-client.private.env.json (ENEDIS_TOKEN).
### mesuresPas is P1D or P1M. grandeurPhysique=PMA returns the single-phase equivalent maximum power.
GET {{ENEDIS_API_PROD}}/mesure_synchrone_auto/v2/puissance_conso_max_quotidienne
    ?pointId=99999999999999&dateDebut=2025-05-01&dateFin=2025-07-14
    &mesuresPas=P1D&grandeurPhysique=PMA
Authorization: Bearer {{ENEDIS_TOKEN}}

### Daily consumption max power — grandeurPhysique=TOUT. On a three-phase PRM this returns one
### grandeur entry per grandeurPhysique (PMA, PMA1, PMA2, PMA3), each with its own points. Use a real
### consented three-phase PRM.
GET {{ENEDIS_API_PROD}}/mesure_synchrone_auto/v2/puissance_conso_max_quotidienne
    ?pointId=99999999999999&dateDebut=2025-05-01&dateFin=2025-07-14
    &mesuresPas=P1D&grandeurPhysique=TOUT
Authorization: Bearer {{ENEDIS_TOKEN}}
